<title>FRANCE: Wrong to say no agreement on EU pact - Chirac.</title>
<headline>Wrong to say no agreement on EU pact - Chirac.</headline>
<dateline>POITIERS, France 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac said on Friday there were still some issues outstanding between France and Germany on a key European Union budget pact, but that it would be wrong to say there was no agreement between the two sides.</p>
<p>Negotiations were going in the right direction, he told a news conference after a one-day Franco-German summit, held three days before European leaders are scheduled to finalise the budget discipline pact informally reached in Dublin last year.</p>
</text>
